      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "is the probability density function for a normally distributed random variable with mean $ \\mu_i $ and variance $ \\sigma_i^2 $. Equation 13.5 has $ 3n - 1 $ parameters to estimate: the $ n - 1 $ mixing proportions $ \\text{Pr}(i) $, and the $ n $ means and variances of the underlying distributions. It is usually assumed that all the variances are equal, reducing the number of unknown parameters to $ 2n $. Various genetic hypotheses allow us to further specify and evaluate the structure of the mixing proportions.",
